Feature: Teams API Integration

  @allure.label.suite:Teams
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: User creates team and can retrieve it
    Given the user is authenticated
    When the user creates a new team via API
    Then the team creation API should return status 200
    And the team should have a valid ID
    When the user retrieves all teams
    Then the newly created team should be in the list

  @allure.label.suite:Teams
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Team owner can invite members and retrieve team members list
    Given the user is authenticated and owns a team
    When the user invites a new member via API
    Then the invitation API should return status 200
    When the user retrieves team members
    Then the invited user should appear with "pending" status
    When the invited user accepts the invitation
    Then the invitee's status should change to "active"

  @allure.label.suite:Teams
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Only team owner can modify team settings
    Given user A is the team owner
    And user B is a regular team member
    When user B attempts to update team settings
    Then the API should return status 403
    When user A updates team settings
    Then the update should succeed with status 200

  @allure.label.suite:Teams
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: User can delete team and it no longer exists
    Given the user is authenticated and owns a team
    When the user deletes the team via API
    Then the deletion should return status 200
    When the user retrieves all teams
    Then the deleted team should not be in the list
